{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"resident-clay-angelfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered during 2dcb-5468. The runaway guard correctly aborts a genuine loop of identical repeated read_file calls (24x in the incident), but nothing steers the model to STOP re-reading before the abort: agent_call.py memo returns cached content plus a passive nudge, cache-hit repeats are not counted toward the runaway window, and no ModelRetry-style hard steer is raised on the Nth identical call. The run burns its budget and truncates its evidence bank, and a fresh re-run can loop again, hurting exit-11 re-run convergence. OSS pydantic-ai practice: raise ModelRetry/ToolFailed on repeated identical tool calls; UsageLimits(tool_calls_limit); prepare_tools/tool_choice=none for tool-free finalization on budget exhaustion. Separate hardening from the 2dcb-5468 misclassification fix; reduces loop frequency / improves convergence but not required for that fault's correctness.","id":"3dde-fd6f-8aa3-4c49","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Runaway/duplicate read_file loop in completion verifier is not steered to stop"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787671497849273001,"uuid":"0e5f1c4a-366a-47ec-b07a-367f22c42bbb"}